.TH WOLFETCH 5 "August 2026" "wolfetch 0.5.4" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
wolfetch \- wolfetch configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration file uses one key=value pair per line.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
theme=royal
show=distro,kernel,host,cpu,memory,disk,uptime
logo=wolf
show_runtime=true
show_process_memory=true
.fi
.SH FIELDS
Fields include distro, kernel, host, wm, de, term, shell, cpu, cpu_usage, gpu,
memory, disk, load, resolution, board and uptime. Use `wm=name` to override
window-manager detection when the session has no marker.
.PP
GPU usage uses AMD or Intel sysfs metrics when available. NVIDIA utilization is
loaded from NVML only with `wolfetch -u`; otherwise unavailable utilization is
reported as `N/A`.
